  "notes": "A1, A2, B1, B2 recorded in New Orleans, Louisiana, in November 1953.\nA3 to A7, B3 to B6 recorded in New Orleans, Louisiana, in 1949.\nThis album was recorded in mono and can be played on any mono or stereo record player.\n\nFrom label: ℗ 1972 Atlantic Recording Corporation (A2, A3, B1 to B4)\n\nA1: Originally issued on [url=https://www.discogs.com/release/5675134]Atlantic 1020[/url] as Professor Longhair & His Blues Scholars.\nA2: Previously unissued take.\nA3, B1 to B4: Previously unissued.\nA4, A7: Originally issued on [url=https://www.discogs.com/release/5675220]Atlantic 906[/url] as Professor Longhair & His Blues Scholars.\nA5, A6: Originally issued on [url=https://www.discogs.com/release/4228151]Atlantic 947[/url] as Roland Byrd.\nB5, B6: Originally issued on Atlantic 897 as Roy \"Baldhead\" Byrd.\nThe album was issued in a gatefold cover.\n\nRunouts are etched. ",
